The Apache-2.0 license on this repository covers the packaging only: the
Dockerfile, the build wiring and the trimmed configuration. The published
artifact itself contains nothing but upstream software, redistributed
under its own terms:

  ModSecurity 3.0.14        Apache-2.0  https://github.com/owasp-modsecurity/ModSecurity
    -> libmodsecurity.so.3 (built from the upstream release tarball)
  ModSecurity-nginx 1.0.4   Apache-2.0  https://github.com/owasp-modsecurity/ModSecurity-nginx
    -> ngx_http_modsecurity_module.so
  nginx 1.27.5              BSD-2-Clause  https://nginx.org/

The two configuration files shipped in conf/ are upstream ModSecurity
files, not original work:

  modsecurity.conf   derived from ModSecurity's modsecurity.conf-recommended
  unicode.mapping    copied verbatim from the ModSecurity source release
                     (extracted at build time from the checksum-verified
                     modsecurity-v${MODSECURITY_VERSION}.tar.gz, so it always
                     matches the engine it ships beside)

